<body>

<div class="badge">PRODUCT OVERVIEW</div>
<h1 class="title">Medical Billing</h1>
<h2 class="subtitle">End-to-end revenue cycle management — from patient intake to claim payment — built into the same platform as your CRM.</h2>

<table class="info">
  <tr><td class="k">Document</td><td>Product Overview — Medical Billing</td></tr>
  <tr><td class="k">Prepared for</td><td>Internal / Stakeholder Presentation</td></tr>
</table>

<h1 class="section">Agenda</h1>
<ul>
  <li><b>Patients &amp; Scheduling</b> — Intake, appointments, encounters</li>
  <li><b>Charges &amp; Claims</b> — Capture, submit, track</li>
  <li><b>Payments &amp; AR</b> — Collections &amp; receivables</li>
  <li><b>Payers &amp; Providers</b> — Insurance, providers, vendors</li>
  <li><b>Inventory &amp; POs</b> — Supplies &amp; purchasing</li>
  <li><b>Documents</b> — Central records repository</li>
  <li><b>Master Data</b> — Configurable reference data</li>
  <li><b>Reports &amp; Dashboard</b> — Operational visibility</li>
</ul>

<h1 class="section">The Big Picture: The Revenue Cycle</h1>
<p>Every stage of getting paid for care — modeled as a connected flow, not disconnected spreadsheets.</p>
<p class="flow">Patient Intake → Appointment → Encounter → Charge Capture → Claim Submission → Payment / Denial → AR &amp; Reporting</p>

<hr class="page-break">

<h1 class="section">Patients &amp; Scheduling</h1>
<ul>
  <li><b>Patients</b> — Central patient records: demographics, history and billing details in one profile.</li>
  <li><b>Appointments</b> — Book, edit and track appointments tied to each patient and provider.</li>
  <li><b>Encounters</b> — Document each visit — the source record that charges are built from.</li>
</ul>

<h1 class="section">Charges &amp; Claims</h1>
<ul>
  <li><b>Charge capture</b> — turn an encounter into billable line items.</li>
  <li><b>Claims workflow</b> — build, review and submit claims to payers.</li>
  <li><b>Denial management</b> — track denied claims and manage appeals in one queue.</li>
</ul>

<h1 class="section">Payments &amp; Accounts Receivable</h1>
<ul>
  <li><b>Payments</b> — Record payer payments against claims.</li>
  <li><b>Patient Payments</b> — Capture co-pays and out-of-pocket collections.</li>
  <li><b>Deposits &amp; AR</b> — Bank deposits reconciled against an aging accounts-receivable view.</li>
</ul>

<hr class="page-break">

<h1 class="section">Payers, Providers &amp; Vendors</h1>
<ul>
  <li><b>Insurance Payers</b> — Maintain the payer directory claims are submitted against.</li>
  <li><b>Providers</b> — Manage the clinicians delivering and billing for care.</li>
  <li><b>Vendors</b> — Track suppliers behind purchase orders and inventory.</li>
</ul>

<h1 class="section">Inventory, Purchase Orders &amp; Accounts</h1>
<ul>
  <li><b>Inventory</b> — Track medical supplies and stock levels.</li>
  <li><b>Purchase Orders</b> — Order from vendors and track fulfillment.</li>
  <li><b>Accounts</b> — Chart of accounts underpinning financial records.</li>
</ul>

<h1 class="section">Documents &amp; Master Data</h1>
<ul>
  <li><b>Documents</b> — A central repository for billing-related files and records, attached where they're needed.</li>
  <li><b>Master Data</b> — Configurable reference data (codes, types, categories) that keeps the whole system consistent.</li>
</ul>

<hr class="page-break">

<h1 class="section">Day-to-Day Workflow</h1>
<ul>
  <li><b>My Work</b> — a personal queue of what needs attention today.</li>
  <li><b>Activity log</b> — a full audit trail of what changed and when.</li>
  <li><b>Reports</b> — operational and financial reporting across the revenue cycle.</li>
</ul>

<h1 class="section">Dashboard</h1>
<p>A single screen for where the money stands — claims in flight, outstanding AR, denials needing attention, and recent payment activity.</p>
<ul>
  <li>Claims status</li>
  <li>AR aging</li>
  <li>Denial rate</li>
  <li>Recent payments</li>
  <li>Provider productivity</li>
</ul>

<h1 class="section">Security</h1>
<p>Sensitive data, handled carefully.</p>
<ul>
  <li><b>Permission-gated screens</b> — billing staff only see the modules their role allows.</li>
  <li><b>Company-scoped records</b> — patient and financial data stays within its own company.</li>
  <li><b>Full activity trail</b> — every change is logged for accountability and audit.</li>
</ul>

<h1 class="section">Technology</h1>
<table class="info">
  <tr><td class="k">Frontend</td><td>Next.js + React</td></tr>
  <tr><td class="k">UI</td><td>Bootstrap-based design system</td></tr>
  <tr><td class="k">Data</td><td>REST API integration</td></tr>
  <tr><td class="k">Shared platform</td><td>Same login &amp; company model as CRM</td></tr>
</table>

<hr class="page-break">

<h1 class="section">Thank You</h1>
<p>Medical Billing — the full revenue cycle, without leaving your CRM.</p>

</body>
</html>
